window.AG_PRACTICE["tongue"] = {"id":"tongue","axis":"dx","seal":"診","scene":"art/scene-clinic.jpg","title":"Tongue Reading","titleZh":"舌象判讀","sub":"Body, coating, moisture, shape — read in that order","subZh":"舌質、舌苔、潤燥、形態——依序而讀","mentor":{"key":"jing","nm":"Jìng Gū","nmZh":"靜姑","line":"\"I cannot see a tongue. So I made my students describe one to me in four sentences: colour of the body, colour of the coat, how thick, how wet. If they could do that, they could diagnose.\"","lineZh":"「我看不見舌頭。所以我要學生用四句話說給我聽：舌質什麼色、舌苔什麼色、多厚、多潤。四句說得清，證就辨得出。」"},"card":{"h":"Body Before Coating 先質後苔","hZh":"","p":"The tongue body reports the state of the organs, the qi and the blood — it changes slowly. The coating reports the pathogen and the stomach qi — it changes fast. Read the body first for the constitution, then the coating for what is happening right now.","pZh":"舌質候臟腑氣血，其變也緩；舌苔候邪氣與胃氣，其變也速。先觀舌質以知其本，後察舌苔以知其標。"},"note":"Photographic plates for this practice are still being made. Until then the descriptions are written out in full — which is, as it happens, exactly the skill a board exam tests. 本練習之舌象照片仍在製作中。目前以文字詳述——而這恰好正是考試所測之能力。","items":[{"k":"mc","q":"Pale tongue body, thin white coating, no other striking feature. What does the BODY colour tell you?","qZh":"舌淡、苔薄白，餘無顯象。舌質之色主何？","opts":[{"t":"Qi and blood deficiency, or yang deficiency","c":"氣血兩虛，或陽虛","ok":1,"note":"A pale body means the tongue is not being filled and warmed — either blood is short, or yang is too weak to bring blood up to the surface. Which of the two you choose depends on whether there are cold signs. 舌淡者，血不充、陽不溫也。血虛抑或陽虛，視有無寒象而定。"},{"t":"Exterior wind-cold","c":"風寒表證","ok":0,"note":"That is read from the *coating* being thin and white together with chills and a floating pulse — not from a pale body, which speaks to the interior. 表證之判在苔薄白，兼惡寒、脈浮。舌質淡者言其裡。"},{"t":"Damp-heat","c":"濕熱","ok":0,"note":"Damp-heat gives a red body with a yellow greasy coat. Nothing here matches. 濕熱者舌紅苔黃膩，與本象不合。"},{"t":"Blood stasis","c":"血瘀","ok":0,"note":"Stasis darkens: a purple or dusky body, sometimes with spots, and engorged veins underneath. 瘀者舌色紫暗，或見瘀斑，舌下絡脈怒張。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Red body with little or no coating, and the surface looks dry. What pattern?","qZh":"舌紅少苔或無苔，且乾。何證？","opts":[{"t":"Yin deficiency with empty heat","c":"陰虛內熱","ok":1,"note":"Three findings, one conclusion. Red = heat. Scant or absent coat = the fluids that grow the coat are gone. Dry = the same shortage seen a second way. Pair it with night sweats, afternoon warmth and a thready rapid pulse and the case is made. 三象一斷：紅為熱，少苔無苔為津液不足以生苔，乾則同一虧損之再見。合盜汗、午後潮熱、脈細數，其證乃立。"},{"t":"Excess heat in the qi level","c":"氣分實熱","ok":0,"note":"Excess heat gives a red body with a THICK dry yellow coat — heat with substance still has a coating. Absence of coating is the tell for emptiness. 氣分實熱者，舌紅而苔黃厚而燥。實熱有形，其苔尚在。無苔者，虛之候也。"},{"t":"Cold-damp","c":"寒濕","ok":0,"note":"Cold-damp gives a pale body with a white greasy coat, usually wet. 寒濕者舌淡苔白膩而潤。"},{"t":"Phlegm-damp","c":"痰濕","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm shows as a greasy coat with substance to it. Here there is almost no coat at all. 痰者苔膩而有形。本案幾無苔可言。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Swollen tongue body with tooth marks along the edges. What does this indicate?","qZh":"舌體胖大，邊有齒痕，主何？","opts":[{"t":"Spleen deficiency with damp retention","c":"脾虛濕盛","ok":1,"note":"The Spleen governs the transformation of fluids. When it is weak, fluid stays in the tissues, the tongue swells, and it presses against the teeth. Pale and swollen leans to yang deficiency; red and swollen leans to damp-heat. 脾主運化水濕。脾虛則水停，舌體胖而受齒之壓。淡胖者偏陽虛，紅胖者偏濕熱。"},{"t":"Liver qi constraint","c":"肝鬱氣滯","ok":0,"note":"Constraint often shows in a normal or slightly dusky body with a wiry pulse; the shape change here belongs to the Spleen. 肝鬱者舌多如常或略暗，其憑在脈弦。形之變當責脾。"},{"t":"Heat entering the blood level","c":"熱入血分","ok":0,"note":"That gives a deep crimson 絳 body, often dry and sometimes with prickles. 熱入血分者舌絳而乾，或起芒刺。"},{"t":"Kidney essence depletion","c":"腎精虧損","ok":0,"note":"Essence depletion tends toward a thin, small tongue rather than a swollen one. 精虧者舌多瘦薄，非胖大。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each coating to what it most often means.","qZh":"舌苔配主病。","pairs":[{"l":"Thin white coat","lZh":"苔薄白","r":"Normal, or an early exterior pattern","rZh":"常態，或表證初起"},{"l":"Yellow coat","lZh":"苔黃","r":"Heat, and the pathogen has gone interior","rZh":"熱證，邪已入裡"},{"l":"Greasy coat","lZh":"苔膩","r":"Damp, phlegm or food retention","rZh":"濕濁、痰飲、食積"},{"l":"Peeled or patchy coat","lZh":"苔剝（地圖舌）","r":"Stomach qi and yin injured","rZh":"胃氣胃陰受損"},{"l":"Thick coat","lZh":"苔厚","r":"The pathogen has substance and depth","rZh":"邪盛而深"}],"note":"Watch the coating over days, not just once. Thin turning thick means the pathogen is advancing; thick turning thin means it is retreating. A coat that vanishes suddenly and completely is a warning about stomach qi, not a sign of recovery. 察苔當觀其變，不可只憑一診。由薄轉厚者邪進，由厚轉薄者邪退。若苔驟然盡脫，乃胃氣之警，非病癒之兆。"},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient's tongue is dusky purple with small dark spots on the sides. What should you consider?","qZh":"舌質紫暗，邊見瘀斑，當慮何？","opts":[{"t":"Blood stasis","c":"血瘀","ok":1,"note":"Stasis darkens the tongue and shows as fixed spots. Look under the tongue as well — engorged, dark, tortuous sublingual veins strengthen the reading considerably. Then ask about fixed stabbing pain that is worse at night. 瘀則舌暗，見斑而有定處。並當觀舌下絡脈：怒張、色深、迂曲者，其證益明。次問刺痛有定處、入夜尤甚。"},{"t":"Yang deficiency","c":"陽虛","ok":0,"note":"Yang deficiency gives a pale, swollen, wet tongue. Purple with spots is a different mechanism, though long-standing yang deficiency can eventually produce stasis. 陽虛者舌淡胖而潤。紫而有斑者機轉不同，然陽虛日久亦可致瘀。"},{"t":"Wind-heat","c":"風熱","ok":0,"note":"Wind-heat gives red edges and tip with a thin yellow coat, in a new illness. 風熱者舌邊尖紅、苔薄黃，且病新起。"},{"t":"Food retention","c":"食積","ok":0,"note":"Food retention shows as a thick, greasy or curdy coat with a sour belch, not as a purple body. 食積者苔厚膩或腐，噯氣酸腐，非舌質紫暗。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which of these can make a tongue reading wrong, and must be excluded first?","qZh":"下列何者可致舌診失實，當先排除？","opts":[{"t":"Staining from food, drink or medicine","c":"染苔","ok":1,"note":"Coffee, black tea, berries, beetroot, turmeric, coloured sweets and some medicines all stain a coating. Ask what the patient ate or drank in the last hour before you commit to a colour. Also check the lighting — natural daylight is best — and that the tongue is protruded relaxed and briefly, since holding it out too long changes the colour. 咖啡、濃茶、莓果、薑黃、有色糖果及某些藥物皆可染苔。定色之前，先問一小時內所食所飲。並注意光線，以自然光為佳；伸舌宜自然、勿久，久則色變。"},{"t":"The patient being older than sixty","c":"年逾六旬","ok":0,"note":"Age changes what is normal but does not falsify the reading. 年高者常態有異，然非失實。"},{"t":"The season","c":"時令","ok":0,"note":"Season shifts the normal picture slightly — a little thicker and damper in late summer — but does not invalidate it. 時令稍移其常，如長夏苔略厚而潤，然不至失實。"},{"t":"The patient having eaten nothing since morning","c":"晨起未食","ok":0,"note":"Fasting is closer to ideal for tongue inspection than a recent meal. 空腹反近於佳，勝於甫食之後。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Thick white greasy coat, pale swollen body, and the tongue is visibly wet. Which reading fits best?","qZh":"苔白厚膩、舌淡胖、舌面水滑。何證最合？","opts":[{"t":"Cold-damp, with Spleen yang failing to move fluids","c":"寒濕，脾陽不運水濕","ok":1,"note":"Every element points the same way: white = cold, greasy = damp with substance, pale and swollen = deficient and waterlogged, wet = fluids sitting still. Expect heavy limbs, a full chest and belly, and a slippery or soft pulse. 諸象同指：白為寒，膩為有形之濕，淡胖為虛而水停，水滑為津液不行。當見肢體困重、胸脘痞滿、脈滑或濡。"},{"t":"Damp-heat in the middle burner","c":"中焦濕熱","ok":0,"note":"Damp-heat turns the coat yellow and the body red. The damp is right; the temperature is not. 濕熱者苔黃而舌紅。濕是而寒熱非。"},{"t":"Dryness injuring the Lung","c":"燥邪傷肺","ok":0,"note":"Dryness gives a dry tongue with a scanty coat — the opposite of wet and thick. 燥者舌乾苔少，與此適反。"},{"t":"Heat in the blood level","c":"熱入血分","ok":0,"note":"That gives a deep crimson tongue, often with no coat at all. 熱入血分者舌絳，多無苔。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Why is the tongue considered so reliable in TCM diagnosis?","qZh":"舌診何以於中醫辨證為可憑？","opts":[{"t":"It is the one place the state of the interior shows directly on the surface","c":"內之虛實寒熱，於此直見於外","ok":1,"note":"Channels and collaterals connect the tongue to the Heart, Spleen, Kidney, Liver and Lung, and it is the only mucosal surface you can inspect without instruments. It also changes with the illness, which lets you track progress visit by visit. 諸經絡脈皆通於舌，心、脾、腎、肝、肺俱有所繫，且為體內唯一不假器械可直觀之黏膜。其象隨病而變，故可逐診而察其進退。"},{"t":"Because it cannot be affected by anything the patient does","c":"以其不為病人所為所動","ok":0,"note":"Untrue, and this is exactly why staining and scraping must be asked about. 非也。正因可為所動，故當問染苔與刮舌。"},{"t":"Because it replaces the pulse","c":"以其可代脈診","ok":0,"note":"Tongue and pulse answer different questions and are read together. When they disagree, that disagreement is itself information. 舌脈所答不同，當合參。二者相違，其違即為消息。"},{"t":"Because every pattern has exactly one tongue picture","c":"以一證必有一舌","ok":0,"note":"Patterns overlap and tongues show mixtures. Read what is there rather than matching to a memorised picture. 證多相兼，舌多見雜象。當實觀其象，不可以記憶之圖相套。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A red tongue tip with a thin coat, in a patient who cannot fall asleep. What does the LOCATION add?","qZh":"舌尖紅而苔薄，其人入睡困難。部位之見主何？","opts":[{"t":"Heart fire — the tip corresponds to the upper burner","c":"心火 — 舌尖候上焦","ok":1,"note":"The tongue is mapped: tip = Heart and Lung (upper burner), centre = Spleen and Stomach (middle burner), root = Kidney (lower burner), sides = Liver and Gallbladder. Red confined to the tip with insomnia points at Heart fire disturbing the spirit. 舌分部候：尖候心肺（上焦），中候脾胃（中焦），根候腎（下焦），邊候肝膽。獨尖紅而失眠者，心火擾神。"},{"t":"Kidney yin deficiency","c":"腎陰虛","ok":0,"note":"The Kidney is read at the root. Kidney yin deficiency also tends to strip the coat rather than redden the tip alone. 腎候於舌根。腎陰虛者多苔少而非獨尖紅。"},{"t":"Liver qi constraint","c":"肝鬱","ok":0,"note":"The Liver is read at the sides. Redness confined to the edges would support that instead. 肝候於舌邊。獨邊紅者方合。"},{"t":"Food retention","c":"食積","ok":0,"note":"Food retention shows in the centre, as a thick or curdy coat. 食積候於舌中，苔厚或腐。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"The coating disappears completely over a few days in a seriously ill patient. How should this be read?","qZh":"重病之人，數日之間苔盡脫，當作何解？","opts":[{"t":"A warning about stomach qi, not a sign of improvement","c":"胃氣之警，非病退之兆","ok":1,"note":"The coating is grown by stomach qi rising. A coat that thins gradually as the patient improves is good; a coat that vanishes suddenly and leaves a mirror-bright surface suggests stomach qi and fluids are failing. Classically this is taken seriously, and in modern practice such a patient needs proper medical assessment. 苔由胃氣上蒸而生。病退則苔漸薄，此為佳；若驟然盡脫，舌面光如鏡，乃胃氣胃陰將竭之候。古來重之，今則當令其就正規醫療評估。"},{"t":"A sign the pathogen has been fully cleared","c":"邪已盡去","ok":0,"note":"Clearance is gradual. Sudden and total loss is a different mechanism. 邪退者其變也漸。驟然盡脫，機轉不同。"},{"t":"Normal variation, of no significance","c":"常有之變，無關緊要","ok":0,"note":"In a seriously ill patient no sudden change is without significance. 重病之人，凡驟變者無可輕忽。"},{"t":"Evidence the treatment was too cooling","c":"藥過寒涼所致","ok":0,"note":"It can be a contributing factor and is worth reviewing, but the finding itself is about stomach qi and needs assessment either way. 過用寒涼或為其一因，宜復審其方；然此象所關者胃氣，無論何因皆當察之。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Cracks running across a red, dry tongue with a scanty coat. What is the usual reading?","qZh":"舌紅而乾、苔少、且見裂紋，常主何？","opts":[{"t":"Fluid and yin depletion","c":"陰津虧損","ok":1,"note":"Cracks appear when the tongue is no longer being moistened. Read with the colour: red and dry with cracks is yin depletion; pale with cracks leans toward qi and blood deficiency. Some people have congenital cracks with no symptoms at all — ask whether it is new. 舌失濡養則生裂。當合其色而讀：紅乾而裂者陰津虧；淡而裂者偏氣血兩虛。亦有先天裂紋而無所苦者，故當問其新舊。"},{"t":"Damp obstruction","c":"濕阻","ok":0,"note":"Damp makes the tongue wet and greasy, not dry and cracked. 濕者舌潤而苔膩，非乾裂。"},{"t":"Exterior pattern","c":"表證","ok":0,"note":"Exterior patterns barely change the tongue body at all in the first days. 表證初起，舌質多無明顯之變。"},{"t":"Cold congealing","c":"寒凝","ok":0,"note":"Cold congealing gives a pale or purple, moist tongue with a white coat. 寒凝者舌淡或紫而潤，苔白。"}]}]};
